          "Now, inspect our standalone Python class `IndAS37ProvisionsEngine`. This platform executes the three core modules of Ind AS 37 for AeroSpace Defense Systems Ltd: 1. Decommissioning Discount Unwinding Module: - Evaluates the $500,000 site rehabilitation obligation maturing in 5 years at an 8% pre-tax discount rate. - Capitalizes initial present value of \\340,291.60$ into property, plant, and equipment. - Computes Year 1 discount unwinding of \\27,223.33, advancing the carrying liability to \\367,514.93. 2. Restructuring Provision Boundary Filter: - Filters a $700,000 enterprise reorganization budget. - Accepts Qualifying Direct Costs: Employee Severance (\\450,000) + Lease Cancellation Penalty (\\120,000) = \\570,000.00$ Provision recognized on the Balance Sheet. - Disallows Ongoing Operating Costs: Retraining (\\80,000) + IT Relocation (\\50,000) = \\130,000.00$, preserving earnings integrity and preventing Big Bath abuse. 3. Legal Claims Tripartite Classification Engine: - Claim A (Supply Breach): Probability 75% (>50%), amount \\200,000 to$ Recognized as a formal Balance Sheet Provision. - Claim B (Patent Infringement): Probability 30% (5% - 50%), amount \\500,000 to$ Disclosed in Notes as a Contingent Liability. - Claim C (Frivolous Lawsuit): Probability 3% (<5%), amount \\100,000 to$ Classified as Remote; zero disclosure required.",
          "Let us trace the complete financial narrative revealed by our simulation. In Module 1, the method `compute_decommissioning_provision` discounts the future \\500,000obligation across 5 years at 8%, capitalizing \\340,291.60 into PPE. It advances time by one year, computing the exact interest unwinding charge of \\27,223.33and growing the balance sheet liability to \\367,514.93. In Module 2, `compute restructuring provision` evaluates the\\700,000corporate turnaround budget, accepting \\450,000 severance and \\120,000lease exit penalties into a \\570,000 qualifying provision while rejecting \\130,000of ongoing retraining and relocation costs. In Module 3, `classify legal contingencies` sorts corporate claims into their strict regulatory buckets: recognizing\\200,000on the balance sheet, disclosing \\500,000 in footnotes, and filtering \\100,000 of remote claims.",
          "Let us review the corporate governance and disclosure mandates under Ind AS 37 Paragraph 84: For each class of provision, entities must present a complete Roll-Forward Table disclosing: 1. Opening carrying amount at the beginning of the period. 2. Additional provisions made in the period, including increases to existing provisions. 3. Amounts used (incurred and charged against the provision) during the period. 4. Unused amounts reversed during the period. 5. The increase during the period in the discounted amount arising from the passage of time (unwinding of discount) and the effect of any change in the discount rate.",
