          "Balance Sheet Presentation under Schedule III: Under Division II of Schedule III of the Companies Act 2013: - The assets of the disposal group classified as held for sale ($31,500,000.00 post-impairment gross assets) must be presented separately from other assets under Current Assets on the face of the Balance Sheet as \"Assets Classified as Held for Sale\". - The liabilities of the disposal group ($4,000,000.00) must be presented separately from other liabilities under Current Liabilities as \"Liabilities Directly Associated with Assets Classified as Held for Sale\". - Offsetting assets and liabilities of a disposal group on the balance sheet is strictly prohibited! - Under Clause 3(i) and Clause 3(xvii) of CARO 2020, statutory auditors verify that proper board authorization was documented, asset impairment was allocated in accordance with Ind AS 36, and that cash losses from discontinued operations are accurately reported. - Under Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, listed enterprises are legally mandated to disclose material divestitures, sales of divisions, or disposal group agreements to stock exchanges (NSE and BSE) within 24 hours of board approval, including the expected date of completion, amount of turnover contributed by such unit, and details of the buyer. - In addition, under Standard on Auditing (SA) 570 (Going Concern), if a divested division generated a substantial portion of operating cash flows, the statutory auditor must evaluate whether the disposal compromises the going-concern viability of the remaining enterprise, or conversely, whether the divestiture successfully restores financial solvency.",
